  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=5{x}^{15}-4{x}^{8}+7{x}^{5}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Here, we apply the addition, constant multiple, and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{15}-4{x}^{8}+7{x}^{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{15})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{8})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7{x}^{5}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{15})-4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{8})+7\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{5}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 15{x}^{(15-1)}-4\\cdot 8{x}^{(8-1)}+7\\cdot 5{x}^{(5-1)} \\\\  & =75{x}^{14}-32{x}^{7}+35{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
